---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import { site } from '../../content/site'
import portrait from '../../assets/photos/ryan-amarit.webp'
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Ryan Amarit is a web lead and product engineer with nine years of building websites, design systems and products."
  palette="about"
>
  <section class="wrap page-hero" data-section="about" data-gl="page">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="page-title" data-split>Strategy to shipped code.</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:2rem">{site.intro}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap about-grid" data-section="about-body">
    <div class="portrait">
      <Image
        src={portrait}
        alt="Ryan Amarit"
        width={1280}
        widths={[480, 720, 960, 1280]}
        sizes="(min-width: 900px) 42vw, 100vw"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="prose-lg">
      <p>
        I lead the web platform at 8am (formerly AffiniPay): eight B2B SaaS brand sites, from 8am.com to
        MyCase and LawPay, that I moved onto one Astro codebase and one Tailwind and Storybook design
        system.
      </p>

      <dl class="facts">
        {site.facts.map((fact) => (
          <div>
            <dt>{fact.label}</dt>
            <dd>{fact.value}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>

      <p>
        Getting there meant moving sites off four different stacks: WordPress, HubSpot, Webflow and
        Gridsome. Now a new page launches 40% faster, and a fix to one component reaches every brand.
        Our 2026 Fall Release won an Awwwards Honorable Mention and a CSSDA Special Kudos.
      </p>
      <p>
        I plan the web team's work with Marketing, Growth, Design, Brand and Content, and I mentor the
        other developer on the team. I also build the Contentful tools that let editors publish without
        waiting on us, and the AI workflows we use for code review and bug fixes.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before 8am I spent three years at Balcom Agency as the developer clients actually talked to: I
        ran discovery, built their sites and trained their teams. Before that, at Fluke, I automated the
        content migration for a global move to Drupal, and it finished ahead of schedule.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside work I'm building RulerIQ, which shows brands what AI assistants say about them. It's
        also where I test how far AI coding agents can go when someone writes the specs, reviews every
        change and won't merge anything that fails its tests.
      </p>

      <p style="margin-top:2.5rem">
        <a class="btn btn-accent" href="/projects/">See the work <span class="btn-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
